From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: rename the shadowed r capture in glm_draft_onepass_tests

tf-cuda-test failed to compile on pin+0001..0031: the DOWN4 check's
`for (...) |*r, v|` capture shadows the function's rng binding `r`
(zig/tests/cuda/glm_draft_onepass_tests.zig:80:59, "capture 'r' shadows local
constant from outer scope"), which the image build's tf-cuda-test compile
surfaces. Renamed to `out`; the rounding arithmetic is untouched.

Gates: the image build glm53-zig:9c9bf54 (fatbins, install, native, sm_121a)
green on spark4, which compiles tf-cuda-test.
diff --git a/zig/tests/cuda/glm_draft_onepass_tests.zig b/zig/tests/cuda/glm_draft_onepass_tests.zig
--- a/zig/tests/cuda/glm_draft_onepass_tests.zig
+++ b/zig/tests/cuda/glm_draft_onepass_tests.zig
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@
         try glm.q4.matmulF32(ks, f32_tile, s, x.ptr, k, xs.ptr, q, wide.ptr, m);
         try s.synchronize();
         try wide.download(0, std.mem.sliceAsBytes(got_wide));
-        for (rounded[0 .. m * n], got_wide[0 .. m * n]) |*r, v| r.* = bf(v);
+        for (rounded[0 .. m * n], got_wide[0 .. m * n]) |*out, v| out.* = bf(v);
         try check.sameBytes("glm-draft-onepass: the fp32 tile rounded against the bf16 tile", std.mem.sliceAsBytes(rounded[0 .. m * n]), got_many[0 .. m * n * 2]);
     }
 }
